1
00:00:04,480 --> 00:00:06,057
Yu-Gi-Oh!

2
00:00:06,140 --> 00:00:09,280
Yu-Gi-Oh! incorporation!

3
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:29,460
Yu-Gi-Oh! Y-Gi-Oh! Y-Gi-Oh! Drew!
Yu-Gi-Oh! You keep the kiss!

4
00:01:06,120 --> 00:01:10,197
that slacker should have been here
10 minutes ago i've got duels to win

5
00:01:10,280 --> 00:01:16,437
here comes joey now hey guys long time
no see hey still in the tournament

6
00:01:16,520 --> 00:01:21,317
wheeler you bet i'm already the
proud owner of two locator cards then

7
00:01:21,400 --> 00:01:27,680
i guess i'm twice as good what you got
four locator cards Awesome job, Mai.

8
00:01:27,900 --> 00:01:29,240
I've got three so far.

9
00:01:29,340 --> 00:01:31,020
Aw, man, I got the least.

10
00:01:32,340 --> 00:01:35,397
How am I ever going to make
it to the Battle City Finals?

11
00:01:35,480 --> 00:01:36,477
Don't worry, Joey.

12
00:01:36,560 --> 00:01:37,917
There's still plenty of time.

13
00:01:38,000 --> 00:01:40,557
You need a total of six locator
cards to get to the finals,

14
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,057
and I know you can do it.

15
00:01:42,140 --> 00:01:45,797
Well, none of us are going to get to the
finals if we're standing around here.

16
00:01:45,880 --> 00:01:46,710
Mai's right.

17
00:01:46,980 --> 00:01:50,037
Watch out, because I'm about
to do some serious catching up.

18
00:01:50,120 --> 00:01:51,767
Good luck and miss me, boys.

19
00:01:52,620 --> 00:01:53,450
See ya.

20
00:01:53,560 --> 00:01:55,717
Luck is for amateurs. Later, Youg.

21
00:01:55,800 --> 00:01:58,388
I know one of Merrick's
hunters is after me.

22
00:01:58,780 --> 00:02:00,180
I'll be ready for him.

23
00:02:03,300 --> 00:02:06,480
I'm watching every move
you make, little Yugi.

24
00:02:11,060 --> 00:02:12,680
Yugi already took off?

25
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:16,508
Yes, he wanted to get an early
start on the tournament today.

26
00:02:16,600 --> 00:02:19,937
I told you to get off the phone
so we could meet him on time.

27
00:02:20,020 --> 00:02:22,917
Yeah, well, I was on an
extremely important call.

28
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:26,200
I needed to take care of
some serious business, Taya.

29
00:02:26,480 --> 00:02:28,277
You mean flirting with serenity.

30
00:02:28,360 --> 00:02:31,277
At this rate, I'm never going
to get to see Yugi duel.

31
00:02:31,360 --> 00:02:32,190
Not true.

32
00:02:32,273 --> 00:02:35,436
I'll slip on my comfy shoes
and help you two find him.

33
00:02:35,720 --> 00:02:39,677
I've got to snag me some of those locator
cards so mine doesn't totally show me up.

34
00:02:39,760 --> 00:02:41,537
But who's going to be my next challenge?

35
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:43,914
I'm ready for anyone who wants to duel.

36
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:46,434
This deck of mine always comes through.

37
00:02:46,900 --> 00:02:48,640
Joey Wheeler? Huh?

38
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:51,337
I knew I recognized you.

39
00:02:51,420 --> 00:02:53,420
Think I could have your autograph?

40
00:02:53,760 --> 00:02:57,777
I can't believe you're just walking
around the street like a regular guy.

41
00:02:57,860 --> 00:02:58,690
Yep, it's me.

42
00:02:58,820 --> 00:02:59,977
So who should I make it out to?

43
00:03:00,060 --> 00:03:00,890
Let's see.

44
00:03:00,973 --> 00:03:02,477
Make it out to my sister, Jessica.

45
00:03:02,560 --> 00:03:03,442
She'll love it.

46
00:03:03,640 --> 00:03:05,437
This will totally blow her mind.

47
00:03:05,520 --> 00:03:06,897
She has a big crush on you.

48
00:03:06,980 --> 00:03:07,810
Yay!

49
00:03:08,960 --> 00:03:09,790
Let's see.

50
00:03:09,873 --> 00:03:11,460
To my adoring fan, Jessica.

51
00:03:11,840 --> 00:03:14,640
That dual disc is so
totally cool. Oh, yeah.

52
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:17,937
I do make this thing look
pretty cool, don't I?

53
00:03:18,020 --> 00:03:19,220
Hey, Joey.

54
00:03:19,520 --> 00:03:21,937
Do you think it would be
okay if I tried it on?

55
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:22,940
Just for a sec.

56
00:03:23,140 --> 00:03:24,537
I promise I'll be careful with it.

57
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:25,450
Okay.

58
00:03:25,533 --> 00:03:27,102
I guess it couldn't do any harm.

59
00:03:28,020 --> 00:03:28,850
Here you go.

60
00:03:28,940 --> 00:03:30,780
Wow, Sands, this is so cool.

61
00:03:31,040 --> 00:03:32,746
Being a toolist is hard work.

62
00:03:32,900 --> 00:03:36,077
You don't just put a tool disc
onto your arm and then presto.

63
00:03:36,160 --> 00:03:37,600
You got exercise.

64
00:03:38,680 --> 00:03:39,900
My tool disc.

65
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:41,857
Get back here, you little rat.

66
00:03:41,940 --> 00:03:43,380
Yugi could be anywhere.

67
00:03:43,780 --> 00:03:44,662
We'll find him.

68
00:03:44,860 --> 00:03:47,213
We have a pretty good view from up here.

69
00:03:47,560 --> 00:03:48,795
Check that out, guys.

70
00:03:49,020 --> 00:03:51,580
You little lying punk. It's a chase?

71
00:03:51,900 --> 00:03:54,429
Looks like some youngsters
are playing tag.

72
00:03:55,480 --> 00:03:56,500
Wait a sec.

73
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,200
Hey, that's Joey.

74
00:03:58,620 --> 00:03:59,855
I got your back, man.

75
00:04:02,080 --> 00:04:04,000
What's the rush? Get off of me.

76
00:04:04,660 --> 00:04:07,037
Tristan, what's he doing
with your dual disc?

77
00:04:07,120 --> 00:04:09,120
That's what I'm about to find out.

78
00:04:10,440 --> 00:04:11,760
I'm really sorry.

79
00:04:12,000 --> 00:04:14,529
I didn't know how else
to become a dualist.

80
00:04:15,400 --> 00:04:16,230
See,

81
00:04:16,313 --> 00:04:21,857
I finally built the deck that I could duel
with When this guy stole all my cards So

82
00:04:21,940 --> 00:04:26,817
you stole someone else's I know it was
wrong I just wanted to be in the Battle City

83
00:04:26,900 --> 00:04:30,997
Tournament That's all The most important
part of being a great duelist Is always

84
00:04:31,080 --> 00:04:32,877
playing with honor There would be no

85
00:04:32,960 --> 00:04:36,040
satisfaction in cheating
your way in You're right,

86
00:04:36,260 --> 00:04:39,497
I'm sorry So who's the punk
that stole your dueling deck?

87
00:04:39,580 --> 00:04:43,260
I don't know He had bug eyes
and a head like a blue beetle

88
00:04:44,180 --> 00:04:45,120
Bug eyes?

89
00:04:45,300 --> 00:04:46,418
Head like a beetle?

90
00:04:46,600 --> 00:04:47,620
Wait a sec.

91
00:04:48,580 --> 00:04:50,480
It's gotta be Weevil Underwood.

92
00:04:50,840 --> 00:04:53,817
I guess Weevil's still up
to his old tricks, eh, Joey?

93
00:04:53,900 --> 00:04:55,371
All right, now I'm angry.

94
00:04:55,580 --> 00:04:56,620
Where is he?

95
00:04:56,820 --> 00:04:59,317
I'm gonna teach that
little bug a thing or two.

96
00:04:59,400 --> 00:05:02,220
He's by the fountain. He's mine. Hold on.

97
00:05:02,760 --> 00:05:04,460
Joey. Goodbye now.

98
00:05:05,120 --> 00:05:06,860
See ya, and good luck.

99
00:05:14,780 --> 00:05:16,300
So, were you successful?

100
00:05:16,880 --> 00:05:17,760
Yep, totally.

101
00:05:18,220 --> 00:05:22,020
I did what you told me to, and
they believed every single word.

102
00:05:22,420 --> 00:05:25,480
Then the fools have
crawled right into my trap.

103
00:05:25,960 --> 00:05:27,380
Weaver is mine.

104
00:05:28,440 --> 00:05:29,697
All right, I did it.

105
00:05:29,780 --> 00:05:31,697
Now give me that rare
card you promised me.

106
00:05:31,780 --> 00:05:33,520
Ah, yes, the rare card.

107
00:05:34,260 --> 00:05:35,090
Awesome.

108
00:05:35,173 --> 00:05:37,900
Hey, it's a stinkin' Gokobor card.

109
00:05:38,120 --> 00:05:40,260
Everybody has this one. Ha!

110
00:05:40,740 --> 00:05:43,840
So you want me to give
you something else? Yeah!

111
00:05:44,240 --> 00:05:47,260
All right, how about a
taste of my arachno-slide?

112
00:05:49,700 --> 00:05:52,700
My plan is coming together perfectly.

113
00:05:53,880 --> 00:05:57,880
Yuki may have defeated my great
Moth in doing this kingdom,

114
00:05:58,260 --> 00:06:02,100
but after the trap I've set,
Whaler won't stand a chance.

115
00:06:16,060 --> 00:06:18,360
Kenta, you can't hide from me.

116
00:06:19,540 --> 00:06:21,937
Serenity, did you hear
anyone come in here?

117
00:06:22,020 --> 00:06:23,137
No, why do you ask?

118
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:24,737
There's a little boy
running around the ward

119
00:06:24,820 --> 00:06:27,017
trying to avoid getting his x-rays taken.

120
00:06:27,100 --> 00:06:28,520
He must be scared.

121
00:06:29,440 --> 00:06:33,734
Yeah, he won't go near the machine,
even though I told him it's painless.

122
00:06:35,600 --> 00:06:37,580
It's okay, you can come out now.

123
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,116
You knew I was here?

124
00:06:40,260 --> 00:06:42,672
I could hear you breathing under the bed.

125
00:06:43,660 --> 00:06:45,597
So, how come you didn't turn me in?

126
00:06:45,680 --> 00:06:48,237
I was kind of scared of
some of the tests here, too.

127
00:06:48,320 --> 00:06:51,614
But, you know, they're not
as bad as you think they are.

128
00:06:51,820 --> 00:06:55,017
There must be something I can do to
pay you back for covering for me.

129
00:06:55,100 --> 00:06:56,720
Any ideas? Huh.

130
00:06:57,900 --> 00:06:59,100
Yeah, I've got it.

131
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:01,577
You could check out the
Battle City website for me.

132
00:07:01,660 --> 00:07:03,100
Sure, but how come?

133
00:07:03,320 --> 00:07:04,908
My brother's dueling today.

134
00:07:05,020 --> 00:07:06,660
He's a duelist? Awesome!

135
00:07:07,820 --> 00:07:10,040
Ah, where is that bug-eyed punk?

136
00:07:10,520 --> 00:07:12,500
That kid said he was around here.

137
00:07:12,820 --> 00:07:14,640
Looking for someone? Huh?

138
00:07:15,860 --> 00:07:18,200
I thought I smelled a dung beetle.

139
00:07:18,440 --> 00:07:21,060
That's my critique after all this time.

140
00:07:22,180 --> 00:07:25,651
You stole that little kid's
cards, didn't you, Worm Breath?

141
00:07:25,740 --> 00:07:28,040
I don't remember stealing any cards.

142
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:31,024
Well, then maybe I can
help refresh your memory.

143
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:32,140
Tristan, wait.

144
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:35,117
We'll settle this fair
and square with a duel.

145
00:07:35,200 --> 00:07:36,920
Be really careful, Joey.

146
00:07:37,220 --> 00:07:40,857
Remember when Weevil threw Yugi's Exodia
cards off the boat to Duelist Island?

147
00:07:40,940 --> 00:07:42,528
This guy's a major cheater.

148
00:07:44,120 --> 00:07:46,277
Careful where you point that finger, Taya.

149
00:07:46,360 --> 00:07:49,160
It might get bitten by
one of my pets. Gross.

150
00:07:50,560 --> 00:07:52,240
All right, let's do this.

151
00:07:52,420 --> 00:07:53,596
That's fine with me.

152
00:07:53,740 --> 00:07:57,180
But we'll duel for two
Locator cards. Two of them.

153
00:07:57,380 --> 00:08:01,397
But if you lose both Locator cards, you'll
have no way of getting to the finals.

154
00:08:01,480 --> 00:08:04,337
It's way too risky, Joey. That's it.

155
00:08:04,420 --> 00:08:06,680
You even have to. That's it.

156
00:08:07,020 --> 00:08:08,300
Be careful, Joey.

157
00:08:08,540 --> 00:08:10,277
Yu-Gi squashed this creepy little bug the

158
00:08:10,360 --> 00:08:12,437
first time they squared
off at Dua's kingdom.

159
00:08:12,520 --> 00:08:14,637
Now I guess it's my turn to do the same.

160
00:08:14,720 --> 00:08:17,320
How many locator cards do you have? Two.

161
00:08:17,860 --> 00:08:21,217
Then once I step on you and take
them both, plus your rarest card,

162
00:08:21,300 --> 00:08:24,757
I'll be personally responsible for kicking
your ugly mug out of the tournament.

163
00:08:24,840 --> 00:08:25,670
Yeah.

164
00:08:25,753 --> 00:08:28,100
Just like Yu-Gi did last time.

165
00:08:30,420 --> 00:08:31,250
Yeah!

166
00:08:34,420 --> 00:08:35,480
Let's do this!

167
00:08:35,940 --> 00:08:37,260
It's time to duel!

168
00:08:37,580 --> 00:08:41,700
First, I'll play my Swordsman
of Landstar in attack mode.

169
00:08:43,060 --> 00:08:46,236
And I'll leave this little
number face down for later.

170
00:08:47,020 --> 00:08:48,560
Take your best shot.

171
00:08:48,840 --> 00:08:51,917
Your Swordsman looks like
he popped out of a toy box.

172
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:54,277
This toy's gonna slice and dice your hide.

173
00:08:54,360 --> 00:08:55,520
Well, is that so?

174
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:59,960
Now I've played a much more powerful
flying commentary number one.

175
00:09:00,900 --> 00:09:03,297
Now, my flying friend, attack!

176
00:09:03,380 --> 00:09:07,600
Crash this mini-monster!
Uh-uh. Watch this.

177
00:09:08,060 --> 00:09:10,680
It's my shield and sword magic card.

178
00:09:10,920 --> 00:09:14,337
It swaps the attack and defense
points of both our monsters,

179
00:09:14,420 --> 00:09:18,008
making my sword ring's attack
strength a cut above your butt.

180
00:09:20,740 --> 00:09:22,160
Oh, nice try!

181
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:25,637
But when flying Kamakiri number
one is sent to the graveyard,

182
00:09:25,720 --> 00:09:29,097
it automatically summons an even more
powerful warrior to take its place,

183
00:09:29,180 --> 00:09:31,680
the dreaded flying Kamakiri number two!

184
00:09:34,960 --> 00:09:37,837
Serenity, your brother's
name is Joey Wheeler, right?

185
00:09:37,920 --> 00:09:38,750
That's it?

186
00:09:39,560 --> 00:09:43,520
Oh, man, it says he's dueling with
a regional champion right now.

187
00:09:44,200 --> 00:09:45,847
Hey, don't sound so worried.

188
00:09:46,200 --> 00:09:50,082
My brother came in second place
in the Duelist Kingdom tournament.

189
00:09:50,500 --> 00:09:51,800
Really? Mm-hmm.

190
00:09:53,480 --> 00:09:55,620
I know Joey will beat this guy.

191
00:09:56,820 --> 00:10:00,467
You're no match for my winged
warrior, so give it up, Wheeler!

192
00:10:02,220 --> 00:10:03,737
Awesome, it's Jinzo,

193
00:10:03,820 --> 00:10:08,197
the card I won from Esperoba Now I just
need to get it on the field Hurry up,

194
00:10:08,280 --> 00:10:11,477
Wheeler My flying
Kamakiri is getting hungry

195
00:10:11,560 --> 00:10:15,520
And it's feeding time Just
ignore him Come on, Joey

196
00:10:16,200 --> 00:10:20,940
No sweat I'll just sacrifice my
swordsman so I can put Jinzo on the map

197
00:10:23,860 --> 00:10:26,919
Jinzo, smash his Kamakiri
like a bug on a windshield

198
00:10:30,880 --> 00:10:31,710
Oh!

199
00:10:31,793 --> 00:10:34,140
That wasn't supposed to happen. Ha!

200
00:10:34,340 --> 00:10:35,817
Eat dirt, you little grub.

201
00:10:35,900 --> 00:10:37,488
Squash that mealworm, Joey.

202
00:10:37,640 --> 00:10:38,640
Here's one more.

203
00:10:38,900 --> 00:10:40,420
In defense mode.

204
00:10:40,700 --> 00:10:42,520
Just try to attack this.

205
00:10:43,020 --> 00:10:47,800
You just set him up and I'll
knock him down. Jinzo, attack!

206
00:10:52,620 --> 00:10:53,560
What's that?

207
00:10:53,960 --> 00:10:56,700
Ah, that's my flying leech, Kisatai.

208
00:10:56,840 --> 00:10:59,477
It attaches itself to the
first monster that attacks it.

209
00:10:59,560 --> 00:11:03,377
Then it increases my life points
by 1,200 every time it's your turn.

210
00:11:03,460 --> 00:11:07,577
So as long as my leech continues to
peen, my life points continue to grow.

211
00:11:07,660 --> 00:11:08,601
That's not cool.

212
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:10,770
Disgusting.

213
00:11:11,900 --> 00:11:15,547
And this is just the beginning
of what I have planned for you.

214
00:11:15,660 --> 00:11:18,117
You've got a lot to learn
about the insect world,

215
00:11:18,200 --> 00:11:20,965
and I'm just the duelist
to teach you, Wheeler.

216
00:11:21,100 --> 00:11:23,806
Now I'll play another
monster in defense mode.

217
00:11:24,340 --> 00:11:25,860
I'll take care of that.

218
00:11:26,140 --> 00:11:28,200
And I'll take more life points.

219
00:11:30,180 --> 00:11:31,840
Thanks to my leech friend.

220
00:11:34,040 --> 00:11:37,628
Jinzo may have a leech on him,
but he can still cyber attack.

221
00:11:41,920 --> 00:11:43,960
You're too kind. Hey, wait.

222
00:11:44,260 --> 00:11:46,560
More life points. That's right.

223
00:11:46,740 --> 00:11:50,977
You attacked my skull mark ladybug,
which gives me an extra 500 life points.

224
00:11:51,060 --> 00:11:53,580
Didn't I tell you you had a lot to learn?

225
00:11:54,860 --> 00:11:57,557
Insect cards can be very, very tricky.

226
00:11:57,640 --> 00:12:01,200
I'm afraid Joey is going to
have to be ready for anything.

227
00:12:01,760 --> 00:12:02,590
Ha!

228
00:12:02,673 --> 00:12:05,246
I'll play yet another
monster in defense mode.

229
00:12:05,780 --> 00:12:09,640
And since it's your turn again,
more life points, please!

230
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:12,797
With my leash feeding on your monster,

231
00:12:12,880 --> 00:12:15,917
my life points will continue to
grow, making me indestructible!

232
00:12:16,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Say goodbye to the Battle
City Tournament, Wheeler!

233
00:12:21,400 --> 00:12:22,880
Now how's Joey doing?

234
00:12:23,200 --> 00:12:26,082
Well, it looks like he's
in kind of a tight spot.

235
00:12:26,220 --> 00:12:28,577
Don't get me wrong, he's
playing really well.

236
00:12:28,660 --> 00:12:30,937
But this Underwood guy
keeps turning things around.

237
00:12:31,020 --> 00:12:34,920
I know my brother can handle
whatever his opponent tries to do.

238
00:12:35,600 --> 00:12:36,640
How do you know?

239
00:12:36,860 --> 00:12:39,417
My brother Joey won't
let anything stop him.

240
00:12:39,500 --> 00:12:41,517
He's been in tough situations before,

241
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:44,365
and he always comes
through and makes me proud.

242
00:12:44,560 --> 00:12:45,736
I hope you're right.

243
00:12:46,020 --> 00:12:49,737
Because if he loses his only two locator
cards, he's out of the tournament.

244
00:12:49,820 --> 00:12:53,037
There's only one thing that my
brother needs to do right now.

245
00:12:53,120 --> 00:12:55,020
He needs to believe in himself.

246
00:12:55,700 --> 00:12:57,080
Here goes nothing.

247
00:12:58,000 --> 00:12:59,440
Ah, this'll help.

248
